WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.186
Hi! What is one quarter plus three eighths? The denominators are different, so can we just add? Today we'll add and subtract related fractions.

2
00:00:12.336 --> 00:00:21.858
First, a reminder: with the same denominator, add the numerators and keep the denominator. Two sevenths plus three sevenths is five sevenths.

3
00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:28.722
4 and 8: 8 is 2 times 4. Fractions like these are called related fractions.

4
00:00:28.872 --> 00:00:32.034
Change one quarter into two eighths.

5
00:00:32.184 --> 00:00:37.194
Two eighths plus three eighths is five eighths.

6
00:00:37.344 --> 00:00:40.914
Work out five sixths minus one third.

7
00:00:41.064 --> 00:00:44.202
Change one third into two sixths.

8
00:00:44.352 --> 00:00:50.946
Five sixths minus two sixths is three sixths. In simplest form, that's one half.

9
00:00:51.096 --> 00:00:59.562
1 minus three eighths: think of 1 as eight eighths. Take away three eighths to get five eighths.

10
00:00:59.712 --> 00:01:06.690
Watch out! Some pupils add the tops and add the bottoms and get four twelfths. That's wrong!

11
00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:14.922
The denominator tells the size of the parts, so we never add it. Make the denominators the same, then add the numerators.

12
00:01:15.072 --> 00:01:20.058
One quarter plus three eighths is five eighths.

13
00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:28.770
Your turn! What is two fifths plus three tenths? Pause and think.

14
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:36.954
Two fifths is four tenths. Add three tenths to get seven tenths. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:37.104 --> 00:01:45.618
Another one! What is one half plus one sixth? Pause and think.

16
00:01:45.768 --> 00:01:55.458
One half is three sixths. Add one sixth to get four sixths, which simplifies to two thirds. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:55.608 --> 00:02:04.410
Here's another! What is seven ninths minus one third? Pause and think.

18
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:13.290
One third is three ninths. Seven ninths minus three ninths is four ninths. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:22.362
Here's another! What is three quarters minus five eighths? Pause and think.

20
00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:30.834
Three quarters is six eighths. Take away five eighths to get one eighth. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:41.082
Last one! Three eighths of a cake was eaten. What fraction is left? Pause and think.

22
00:02:41.232 --> 00:02:50.298
The whole cake is 1, or eight eighths. Take away three eighths and five eighths are left. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:50.448 --> 00:03:01.866
Remember: to add or subtract related fractions, make the denominators the same, add or subtract the numerators, keep the denominator, and simplify at the end.

24
00:03:02.016 --> 00:03:07.098
When you eat pizza, work out what fraction is left!

